# validate-scope-dod-progress baseline — Research Lab
#
# Scopes whose state.json progress claim does NOT match the Definition-of-Done
# rows of the artifact it summarises, plus claims whose artifact cannot be
# located at all. Frozen so the guard can fail on NEW drift while this
# pre-existing set is reconciled.
#
# Keyed on `<packet>#<ordinal>::<registry array>`, NOT on the numbers. A scope
# already listed here stays frozen until it is reconciled, so re-freezing
# cannot be used to accept a new wrong number; a scope NOT listed here FAILS
# the moment its claim and its artifact disagree. That is the regression this
# guard exists to stop.
#
# The two registry arrays are listed separately on purpose: when
# `execution.scopeProgress` and `certification.scopeProgress` disagree, exactly
# one of them is the stale one, and collapsing them would hide which.
#
# THIS LIST MUST SHRINK, NEVER GROW. Every entry is paid down by one of:
#   - reconcile the claim against the artifact, in the owning packet, or
#   - give the scope a Definition of Done the claim can summarise, or
#   - drop a count claim the packet cannot substantiate
# Never by ticking a checkbox to match the number.
#
# A baseline entry that is no longer drifted is reported as STALE and the run
# still exits 0. Remove it. Do NOT regenerate the baseline to silence a
# genuine new finding.
#
# Regenerate ONLY when deliberately accepting the current set:
#   node scripts/validate-scope-dod-progress.mjs --update-baseline
#
# There is no --skip / --force / --ignore / --bypass flag and there never will
# be. A bypass-shaped flag exits non-zero.
#
# FROZEN: 14 finding(s) — 14 drifted, 0 unresolvable — of 85 claim(s) across 62 packet(s), on 2026-08-25.
#
